svg: honour class selectors from a <style> sheet (#2155)

The SVG parser only read presentation attributes and the inline style
attribute, so Illustrator/Inkscape output that keeps all its colors in a
<style> sheet and references them with class="st0" rendered every shape
with the default fill: solid black.

Collect the ".name { ... }" rules of every <style> element at document
open time and splice the matching declarations onto the element's style
attribute before parsing it. Inline declarations come first, so they
still win over the sheet. Anything more than a plain class selector
(at-rules, element and id selectors, combinators, pseudo classes) is
skipped rather than half-supported.
